<title>UK: German inland gas oil eases, demand steady.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil eases, demand steady.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.5162)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     37.20/37.50     24.53/24.73     37.90/38.20</p>
<p> BREMEN		37.20/37.50     24.53/24.73     37.90/38.20</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    37.70/38.00     24.86/25.06     38.00/38.40</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   38.30/38.60     25.26/25.45     38.80/39.10</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   38.40/38.70     25.32/25.52     38.90/39.20</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  39.40/39.70     25.98/26.18     39.90/40.20</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices retreated in sympathy with futures on Monday but end-user demand was steady with colder temperatures and a firmer dollar arousing bullish sentiment. London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
